  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Poopship (13:16)** (1 review): Reviewer singles out Poopship Destroyer running into Ballad of the Pooples as Ween near their peak [10]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Back To Bason (4:47)**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [12]\n- **Bannannas and Blow (3:20)**: rare: 3 archived performances [12]\n- **Ooh Vala (4:55)**: back after 60 archived shows (449 days) [12]\n- **B-day Boy * (4:42)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **Gonna Be A Long Night (3:14)**: rare: 3 archived performances [12]\n- **Poopship (13:16)**: back after 178 archived shows (1484 days); rare: 7 archived performances [12]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2004-06-13.mc012.ua5.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 33 songs; 172 min; rated 5/5 by 10 [1]. Said about its sound: Uploader says the tape came out quite well, though he struggled to stay awake during the hard-rock set [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Set was scheduled for June 12 but began after midnight, in the early hours of June 13, 2004 [1]\n- A friend, Boardmonkey, guarded the taper's spot and stopped a spun festival-goer from tumbling between the taper's stand and others [1]\n- Warm Tennessee night with huge energy in the tent; people ran from hundreds of yards away to see the commotion [5]\n- Attendee was too intoxicated to record, and remembers playing air guitar with a folding chair [9]\n- Reviewer calls this the highlight of that year's Bonnaroo [4]\n- Reviewer rates it the best moment of any festival they have attended [5]\n- Reviewer, at a first Ween show, found it the highlight of Bonnaroo 2004 and intensely wild [6]\n- Reviewer says the White Pepper tour was looser and more fun, but 2004 and this show were Ween's tightest [10]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Ween2004-06-13.mc012.ua5.flac16**: taped by \"Scuba\" Jeremy; transferred by \"Scuba\" Jeremy; source: Oktava MC012 Cardioid approx. ORTF > UA5 (48Khz) > PCM-M1 [1]",
